  "notes": "A compound of {遠|とお}い (far) and {出|で} (going out). Functions as both a noun and a suru-verb.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {遠出|とおで}する (to go on an excursion)\n- {遠出|とおで}の{予定|よてい} (plans for an outing)\n- {少|すこ}し{遠出|とおで}する (to go a little farther than usual)\n- {遠出|とおで}ができない (can't go far)\n\nLess formal than {旅行|りょこう} (travel) and implies a shorter, more casual trip — like a day trip or weekend outing rather than a formal vacation. Often used when someone ventures a bit beyond their usual neighborhood or daily routine.",
